{
  "description": "Checking a goods receipt before it is posted (PUR-02, W1-16). Problems block posting: the header (supplier, the supplier's bill number and date, the location, at least one line), each line (an item, a quantity above 0, whole for a unit without fractions, a unit cost of 0 or more in whole paisa, a line discount of 0 up to its gross), the bill discount (0 up to Σ nets), then the bill total as printed: required, and equal to the computed total (the difference = printed − computed). Warnings don't block: a net unit cost more than 10 % above or below the item's last cost, and Retail at or below the net unit cost. Rows are 0-based; null = the receipt. Totals and the difference are null when a line or a discount is invalid. W2-17 (owner answer 1): with `maxAmount` (Rs 1 crore in minor units), a unit cost over it is cost_too_large, a quantity × cost over it line_too_large, the bill total as printed or the lines together over it total_too_large; a quantity over what the books hold (99,999,999,999.999) is qty_too_large. Without `maxAmount` the limit is the safe-integer range. Nothing too large is ever thrown: it is a problem. W2-18: with `billNoPostedAs` (the number of a posted receipt that already has this supplier's bill), the receipt has the header problem bill_no_taken, right after the bill number's own; it stops Post, not Save draft.",
